<!--
  ~ Android TV size tokens, from the 1920x1080 TV mock (Main, Settings, Token).
  ~ Every value here is a mock pixel measure times one factor; the three
  ~ files differ only in that factor, so the design keeps its proportions
  ~ whatever density the TV reports (xhdpi: 1920x1080 px is 960x540 dp, one mock pixel is half a dp).
  ~ The TV layouts use nothing else for size, which is what makes that work.
  ~ Generated from one table of mock pixels: change a measure in all three
  ~ files at once, keeping value = px x factor (rounded to half a dp).
  ~
  ~ The *_view_* tokens are the halo at work: focus draws a ring and a halo
  ~ outside the element, as the mock's box-shadow does, and a background
  ~ cannot paint outside its view. So a focusable view is its visible size
  ~ plus a halo on every side (the drawables keep the resting look inset by
  ~ the halo), and neighbours overlap by what the visible gap leaves over.
  ~ A focusable view never sticks out of its parent, which would clip its
  ~ halo: the views beside it that do not take focus are moved in by a halo
  ~ instead, so the visible edges still line up.
  -->
